course: dictionary
lesson: 9573
title: Strangler: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. «A strangler fig starts from a seed dropped high on a tree by a bird.» Words like fig, seed, tree and roots tell you that strangler here means a plant, not a person.
explain: A strangler is a person who kills or hurts someone by squeezing their throat so they cannot breathe. Crime news and detective stories use this meaning. The action word is strangle, and the naming word for the act is strangulation.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning. If it does not, look at the other clues around the word.
fact: Strangler is a noun: one strangler, two stranglers. Its related words are strangle (a verb, to squeeze someone's throat) and strangulation (the act of doing it).
fact: A strangler fig is a tropical plant. It starts as a seed high in a tree, grows roots down to the ground, and wraps around its host.
fact: Weeds that wrap around and choke other plants are sometimes called stranglers.
fact: In crime news, "the strangler" is a nickname for a violent criminal, and it tells the reader the story is about serious crime.
fact: Safety: never put anything around anyone's neck, even in play.
exercise: «A strangler fig starts from a seed dropped high on a tree by a bird.» In this sentence, what is a strangler fig? | *A tropical plant that grows around a tree | A tall tree with big leaves | A bird that eats seeds | A kind of fish
exercise: «A strangler fig sends roots down to the ground and wraps the host.» In this sentence, what is the host? | The ground under the roots | The bird that dropped the seed | The seed | *The tree the fig grows around
exercise: In crime news, "the strangler" is a nickname for a violent criminal. What does this tell the reader? | *The story is about serious crime | The story is a funny picture book | The story is about a garden | The story is about the weather
test: Strangle is a related word of strangler. What kind of word is strangle? | A number | A colour | *A verb, an action word | A noun, a naming word
test: «Weeds that wrap around and choke other plants are sometimes called stranglers.» What does choke mean here? | Give them more sunshine | Dig them up for food | Help them grow tall | *Stop them growing well by wrapping tightly around them
exam: Why must you never put anything around anyone's neck, even in play? | *Squeezing someone's neck can stop them breathing and seriously hurt them | It helps them sleep | It makes them laugh | It makes the game more fun
